ally  special that i get to be that person  that i never really had to look up to um  and i hope that i'm an inspiration to  others and um and i hope that i spread a  message that if i can do it you can do  it  enter what was it like for you to join  the show and take on this role what were  you most nervous about and what made you  feel most reassured once you got on set  everyone was super supportive and kind i  remember the first scene  you know doing something new can always  be a little scary but with the help of  your friend you can always get through  it um and  it was just wonderful really connecting  with all the girls we built a wonderful  relationship and  yeah it's truly been a dream filming  so what's it like to play the leader of  this group is that a role that you fit  into naturally what sort of leader would  you say she is in season two  well just like christy i'm also  extremely independent and  uh but christy chrissy really is a  natural leader she she knows how to work  with people and she knows how to get  what she wants and also compromise  she is assertive and she is  punctual she's just really admirable in  the sense that she knows who she is and  she knows what she wants  malia what's it like for you with your  character you know things are changing a  little bit with her family what is it  like for her how does she feel about  what's going on with that situation  yeah marianne i mean she turned on one  of these stepsisters so much it's crazy  we go to such lengths and such extents  to becoming stepsisters and there's  always that tease of is it finally going  to happen are they going to announce  what they just proposed or  is it something else then this one a  case is it something like that and i get  to see that throughout the second season  and throughout john's night's episodes  in particular i think that's really fun  to be able to portray um but the course  of the first season marianne has a huge  arc and throughout the second season 